# OpenSpec change citations

Name an OpenSpec change only in `openspec/`, `DESIGN_NOTES.md` and `design/`.

Do not cite a change id (`05c-play-shell`), a change number (`Change 06`, `Changes 09 & 09a`), or "this change" in `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, source, tests, or comments. Describe the module.

Root `AGENTS.md` and root `README.md` may explain how to run OpenSpec (`/opsx-propose`, `/opsx-apply`, `/opsx-archive`, `npx openspec`). That is the workflow, not a change.

```text
Bad:  MessageTransitQueue — Change 06
Good: MessageTransitQueue
Bad:  three (Change 4)
Good: three
```

The verb "change" (`set_separation_weight`) is not a change id.
